<!--
  CLI Documentation — TransformCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.TransformCommand
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:transformer="org.blockml.bml.transformer"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>TransformCommand</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:TransformCommand</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>blockml transform specification</is>

  <documentation><![CDATA[Syntax:
    blockml transform apply EXECUTION-FQN [--verbose] [--parameters JSON]

    transform is a parent command. V1 defines the apply subcommand only.
    Further transform subcommands are declared on clicommand:TransformCommand
    subcommands.

    EXECUTION-FQN is the FQN of a ModelTransformation under
    {library}._meta.transform.pending. Tasks are not accepted directly.

    --parameters is a JSON object merged over pending ModelTransformation
    parameters (CLI wins; nested objects merge; arrays replace). Prepare
    checks the result against the bound generic T (default type:EmptyStruct)
    and writes it onto the running copy. Omitted --parameters is {}.

    The transformer takes an exclusive worktree lock, then prepares the
    ModelTransformation and runs each workflow Stage in order: persist
    Stage Running, Execute its Task in an isolated agent process, Reflect,
    Persist results onto that Stage. Default Prepare/Finalize are
    deterministic. Default Execute is a TransformationAgent (Claude Code)
    that changes BML only. Default Reflect is a second Claude worker
    (read-only; changedFiles + feedback). Default Persist writes those
    fields onto the Stage. Finalize relocates to _meta.transform.succeeded
    only when every Stage succeeded; otherwise _meta.transform.failed and a
    non-zero exit. A failed Stage aborts the rest.

    Lifecycle lines (ModelTransformation and Stage status, execute/reflect
    start and done) always print so progress is visible without --verbose.

    Only one transform may run at a time in the same Git worktree. A second
    call fails immediately (exit 2) with no wait. Different worktrees may
    run in parallel.

    --verbose streams additional agent-session detail (thinking, tools, text).
    It does not control the lifecycle lines.

    The worktree must be clean at start and before each Stage (exit 2
    otherwise). Prepare records baseCommit from HEAD and commits the
    running relocation. Each Stage commits Running first, then commits
    model changes with the Stage terminal state. Finalize commits the
    succeeded or failed relocation.

    Pending-contract violations never start the execution (exit 2).

Printed help:
Usage: blockml transform apply <execution-fqn> [--verbose] [--parameters json]
       blockml transform --help

When: run a pending ModelTransformation.

transform is a parent command. V1 defines apply only.
EXECUTION-FQN is the FQN of a ModelTransformation under {library}._meta.transform.pending. Tasks are not accepted directly.

Pipeline stage constraints belong to the Execute / Reflect prompts, not here.

Flags:
  --verbose         stream additional agent-session detail
  --parameters json JSON object merged over pending parameters

Only one transform may run at a time in the same Git worktree.
The worktree must be clean at start and before each Stage.

Related: validate, inspect.]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:TransformCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:TransformApplyCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:RunTransform" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>

</block>
